==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|rōr}}, from {{inh|de|goh|rōr}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*rauza-}}, possibly from {{inh|de|ine-pro|*resg-||to plait, wattle}}, see also {{cog|ga|rusg||bark}}, {{cog|la|restis||rope}}, {{cog|lt|rezgis|režģis|basketwork}}, {{cog|sh|rògoz||sc=Latn|reed}}, {{cog|grc|ἄρριχος||basket}}, {{cog|fa|رغزه|tr=raɣza||woollen cloth}}.

Germanic cognates include {{cog|hrx|Roher}}, {{cog|da|rør}}, {{cog|sv|rör}}.

